Swanirbhar AI Workbench is a secure, air-gapped and sovereign Agentic AI platform designed for confidential industrial environments such as PSUs, defence organizations, refineries, manufacturing units and critical infrastructure. The platform addresses a major limitation of conventional cloud-based AI systems: the requirement to transfer sensitive organizational information to external services.

Swanirbhar follows a Zero Data Egress architecture in which confidential documents, scans, engineering drawings, internal SOPs, manuals, reports and generated outputs remain within the organization's controlled infrastructure. It uses open-weight multimodal Large Language Models hosted locally through Ollama, enabling AI functionality without dependence on external cloud AI APIs or continuous internet connectivity.

Unlike a conventional chatbot, Swanirbhar functions as an AI workbench capable of planning and executing multi-step tasks. Users can submit queries, documents, scans or drawings through a secure desktop interface. The system validates the input, plans the task using an agentic workflow, routes the task to an appropriate local AI model, retrieves relevant organizational knowledge through Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), executes required tools or code inside an isolated Docker sandbox, validates the generated output and provides a final deliverable for user review.

The platform incorporates LangGraph and LangChain for agent orchestration, FastAPI for backend services, PySide6 for the desktop interface, Ollama for local model serving, ChromaDB for knowledge retrieval, Guardrails for input and output protection, Docker for isolated execution, and Langfuse/ELK Stack for monitoring and auditability.

A key feature of Swanirbhar is model-agnostic routing, allowing organizations to add, replace or upgrade open-weight models without redesigning the complete platform. The system also introduces case-based access boundaries where documents, knowledge and activities can remain associated with specific industrial cases or projects.

Security is embedded throughout the workflow through input validation, guardrails, controlled tool access, sandboxed execution, output validation, human-in-the-loop review and activity logging. This enables organizations to use AI for confidential automation while maintaining control, traceability and oversight.

Swanirbhar is designed to generate practical deliverables rather than only conversational responses. Depending on the task, it can produce DOCX reports, XLSX spreadsheets, PPTX presentations, structured analysis and working code.

The proposed solution can reduce manual effort in routine document-intensive workflows, accelerate report and analysis generation, enable private organizational knowledge retrieval and support secure AI adoption in environments where confidentiality and data sovereignty are critical.

Overall, Swanirbhar aims to establish a scalable foundation for sovereign Agentic AI by combining on-premise multimodal AI, RAG, autonomous task planning, secure execution, model-agnostic routing, validation and human oversight into a single controlled industrial AI workbench.
